DOCUMENT 1 — Release Notes (v0.8.1.3.0)
Purpose

Introduce a Day Follow-Through Gate for Scenario B to stand down on weak momentum days, reducing clustered loss days by adding a day-level participation filter (not changing trade-level logic).

What shipped
1) Scenario B: new day-level gate config (scenarios.json)

Added three Scenario B parameters:

require_day_follow_through (bool)

day_follow_through_minutes (int)

day_follow_through_min_symbols (int)

Final configuration for this release:

require_day_follow_through = true

day_follow_through_minutes = 20

day_follow_through_min_symbols = 2

2) Backtester: day gate prepass + sticky daily decision

Implemented a single prepass at the start of each backtest day to decide PASS/FAIL for the day. If FAIL:

No new entries are allowed for the remainder of the day (open-position logic unchanged).

3) Follow-through definition (final v1)

A symbol counts toward day follow-through only if it qualifies in the late window and is not overextended and is liquid.

Late window:

j_start = i_eval - 5, i_eval = day_follow_through_minutes

Only bars j ∈ [j_start..i_eval] can qualify.

VWAP extension cap (reuses existing knob):

Must be within vwap_extension_max_pct (Scenario B already uses 1.5%)

Applies to both:

close_gt_vwap branch

green_body branch

Liquidity floor (fixed constant in code):

Cumulative volume by the qualifying bar must be cum_v >= 50,000.

4) Observability

Added logs:

DAY_GATE: CHECK enabled=... minutes=... min_symbols=... universe=...

One per-symbol line: DAY_GATE: SYM ... including rule, VWAP metrics, absolute VWAP distance, cap, and cum_v

Final: DAY_GATE: PASSED symbols=N or DAY_GATE: FAILED symbols=N ...

Results (what we saw in this thread)
Single-day spot checks

2025-08-06: PASS → trades=4 → +48.74

2025-08-07: FAIL → trades=0 → +0.00 (stand-down works)

2025-08-08: PASS → trades=3 → −41.94 (known “false pass” day)

Range run (Aug-05 → Aug-09; Aug-09 weekend skipped)

TOTALS: trades=11, wins=6, losses=5, winrate=54.55%, totalPnL = −7.46

Key: Gate demonstrably blocks at least one loss cluster day (Aug-07), but does not yet prevent all bad days (Aug-08).

Known limitation (explicit)

The Day Gate v1 can still PASS days that later trade poorly (example: 2025-08-08), because the early “tape health” proxy (2 qualifying symbols at minute ~20) can still be satisfied on a later-failing day.